ons, assumptions and covers sit under `ifdef FORMAL: responses low after reset, B and R stable until taken, B/R rise only one cycle after an accepted request, response codes follow the decode, and never two half-writes held at once.", "entry": "axi4_lite_regs"}, {"path": "axi4_lite_regs_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "axi4_lite_regs_tb: directed self-checking testbench", "summary": "Self-checking testbench for the verification list in section 8 of [artifact:prj-f3241395ae.interface-spec.a1] and the method in section 7 of [artifact:prj-f3241395ae.microarchitecture.a1]. It drives inputs on the falling edge and decides handshakes before the rising edge. Expected data and responses come from a byte-merge model of the stimulus. Scenarios: reset values; write then read of every register; partial and all-zero wstrb; AW before W, W before AW, and both together; B and R back-pressure with checks that the payload holds; back-to-back transfers, including ready on the cycle after a response; SLVERR on unmapped writes and reads; a read and a write on the same clock; reset while B and R are pending; reset that discards a half-accepted AW or W; and a latency check of at most 2 cycles on every transaction. Every failure is reported with $error, and passing checks are counted. The verdict line uses the nirmaan_nonce plusarg and is printed once before $finish; a watchdog prints a failing verdict if the run hangs.", "entry": "axi4_lite_regs_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["I have not run lint, simulation, synthesis or formal tools on these files. Whether they are lint-clean, pass simulation or synthesize without latches is for the platform's lint.run, simulator.run and synth.run to establish.", "I believe the RTL is free of Verilator -Wall warnings and infers no latches, because every combinational output is defaulted at the top of its block and every case has a default. This is unverified.", "Both files carry `timescale 1ns / 1ps so that Verilator does not raise TIMESCALEMOD